{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShJZ2TNKXDSL4HFJp45NmH","type":"tool_result","content":"src:\nassets.d.ts\nbuildinfo.ts\ncli/\ncli.ts\nconfig/\ncontext/\ncredentials/\nfsutil/\ngate/\ngit/\ngocompat/\nlauncher.ts\nllm/\nprompts/\nrecord/\nrender/\nreview/\nrunbundle/\nscope/\nskill/\nsnapshot/\nstartup.ts\ntextsafe/\ntrust/\nutil/\n\nsrc/cli:\ncommand.ts\ncommands.ts\nconfig.ts\ndoctor.ts\nerrors.ts\ngate.ts\nignore.ts\ninit.ts\nlog.ts\nlogin.ts\nlogout.ts\nopenrouter-login.ts\nopenrouter-reply.ts\nprocess.ts\nresolve.ts\nreview-flags.ts\nreview.ts\nrun.ts\nruns.ts\nskill.ts\nsnapshot-meta.ts\nterminal.ts\ntrust.ts\n\nsrc/snapshot:\ndenylist.ts\n\ntest:\ncheck-pack.test.ts\ncli/\nconfig/\ncontext/\ncredentials/\ndiff/\nfsutil/\ngate/\ngit/\ngocompat/\nhelpers/\nindex.ts\nlauncher.test.ts\nlive/\nllm/\nmanifest.test.ts\nprepublish.test.ts\nprompts/\nrecord/\nrelease-fixture.ts\nrelease.test.ts\nrender/\nreview/\nrunbundle/\nscope/\nskill/\nsnapshot/\ntextsafe/\ntooling/\ntrust/\nutil/\nversion.test.ts\n\ntest/cli:\ndoctor.ts\nenv.ts\nerrors.ts\ngate-settings.ts\ngate.ts\nignore.ts\ninit.ts\nlog.ts\nlogin.ts\nlogout.ts\nopenrouter-login.ts\nprocess.ts\nrequire-trust.ts\nreview-config.ts\nreview-errors.ts\nreview-flags.ts\nreview-records.ts\nreview-trust.ts\nreview-units.ts\nreview.ts\nrun.ts\nruns.ts\nskill.ts\nstored-keys.ts\nterminal.ts\ntrust.ts\n\ntest/snapshot:\ndenylist.ts\n.scratch/ts-rewrite:\nissues/\nlearnings.md\nlogs/\nprogress.md\nreview.md\nspec/\nspec.md\n\n.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec:\n00-decisions.md\n01-cli.md\n02-config.md\n03-trust-credentials.md\n04-scope.md\n05-context.md\n06-llm-protocols.md\n07-agent-loop.md\n08-finder-prompts.md\n09-verify-render.md\n10-records.md\n11-snapshot.md\n12-gate.md\n13-login.md\n14-doctor-init-skill.md\n15-packaging.md\n# Scope, context, and exploration tools (TS)\n\n`src/scope/` (public surface in `index.ts`), `src/context/`,\n`src/snapshot/`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Every `git diff` argument list starts with `DIFF_CONFIG` (use\n  `diffArgs(...)` in `src/scope/git.ts`); git rejects an empty\n  `diff.orderFile=`, so it is `/dev/null`.\n- Patch output goes through `gitPatch` (streams into a\n  `SectionCapper`), never the buffered runner.\n- `build` takes the git environment as `BuildOpts.env` (the CLI\n  context's env).\n- The secret denylist lives once in `src/snapshot/denylist.ts`; scope,\n  context, and snapshot import it.\n\n## Context\n\n- Every function that runs git or reads files takes a trailing\n  `ContextOpts` (`signal`, `env`); pass the CLI context's env, and the\n  repo env in tests. `pinIndexTree` reads `GIT_INDEX_FILE` from that\n  env, not `process.env`.\n- Blocking git calls use the shared runner; streamed reads use\n  `gitStream` / `gitCapped` (`src/context/git.ts`).\n- Grounding and normalization work on `Buffer`s; decode to text only in\n  `snippet.ts` (model-facing).\n- Exploration tools (`src/context/tools.ts`): `explorationTools(repo,\n  tree, {env})`; each `run(args, signal)` returns a plain object, a\n  model-caused failure is `{error}`, abort rejects.\n- When stopping a `gitStream` early, `await lineReader.close()` before\n  awaiting `done`: a paused stdout keeps the child's `close` from\n  firing.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Use `newRepo()` (`test/scope/helpers.ts`): a temp repo with its own\n  HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, and `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` file\n  (`repo.globalConfig`, safe to fill with hostile config), passed as\n  `env:repo.env`.\n- APFS refuses non-UTF-8 file names; stage such a name with\n  `git update-index --index-info` to test it on macOS.\n- Memory bounds: plain RSS growth reflects V8 GC timing on discarded\n  pipe chunks, not what code keeps alive. `test/scope/huge.ts` forces gc\n  (`v8.setFlagsFromString('--expose-gc')`, `vm.runInNewContext('gc')`)\n  and bounds `heapUsed + external`.\n- Abort tests put a pid-recording fake `git` first on the env's `PATH`\n  (`wrapGit` in `test/context/bounds.ts`).\n- Tool tests call tools through `call(repo, tree, name, args)` and fake\n  git with `fakeGit` / `onArg` (`test/context/tools-helpers.ts`).\n- Captured-worktree tests build the tree with plumbing (temporary\n  `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, `read-tree HEAD`, `add`, `write-tree`). `write-tree`\n  or `status` on the live index rewrites it, so snapshot the index bytes\n  after those calls when asserting it is unchanged.\n# TypeScript rewrite\n\nApplies to `src/`, `test/`, and `scripts/`. Notes for one area are in\nthat area's file (index in `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Tooling\n\n- `npm test` runs `typecheck`, then bundles and runs the tapzero suite.\n  A new test module must be imported from `test/index.ts`. esbuild drops\n  unused imports without resolving them, so only `typecheck` catches a\n  broken import.\n- `npm run test:one -- test/<area>/<file>.ts` bundles one test module\n  to `test/one-bundle.js` and runs it through tap-spec. Test modules\n  cannot run directly under Node: their `.js` import specifiers only\n  resolve once bundled. It does not typecheck; run `typecheck` too.\n- Lint with `npm run lint`: it preloads `scripts/eslint-ts6.ts`, which\n  gives eslint the TypeScript 6 API because typescript-eslint throws on\n  the TypeScript 7 that `typecheck` uses.\n- Legacy launcher and release files are excluded by name from lint (the\n  `--ignore-pattern` list) and typecheck (`tsconfig.json` `exclude`);\n  the launcher compiles with `tsconfig.launcher.json`.\n- Node runs `scripts/` directly (type stripping), so they use only\n  erasable syntax: no enums, namespaces, or parameter properties.\n- `baseOptions` in `scripts/esbuild-options.ts` holds the esbuild\n  options every bundle shares (text loaders for `.tmpl`, `.md`, `.sh`;\n  `mainFields: ['module', 'main']`, which `jsonc-parser`'s UMD build\n  needs); `scripts/bundle.ts` adds the `require` shim banner. A test\n  that bundles code itself uses both.\n- `npm run bundle` also writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`\n  (`scripts/licenses.ts`) and fails, naming the package, when a bundled\n  package lacks an allowlisted `license` field or a license file. A new\n  runtime dependency must pass it; extending `ALLOWED_LICENSES` needs\n  maintainer approval. `@substrate-system/debug` fails it today, so no\n  `src/` module may import it yet.\n\n## Source conventions\n\n- Keep source ASCII: write `\\uXXXX` escapes. Some editing tools decode\n  escapes into literal characters when writing; check with\n  `grep -nP '[^\\x00-\\x7f]'` after writing a file. eslint `--fix`\n  (quote-props) rewrites a quoted `'\\u00e9'` object key into a literal\n  non-ASCII identifier; put such keys in a const and use a computed key.\n- eslint rejects control characters in regex literals\n  (`no-control-regex`) and labeled statements (`no-labels`); scan char\n  codes and use helper functions instead.\n- Startup guards live in `src/startup.ts`, not `src/cli.ts`: importing\n  the entry runs the CLI, so testable helpers sit in other modules.\n- Module-level swappable functions use a mutable hooks object plus a\n  delegating export (`terminalHooks`, `skillHooks.lookPath`), because\n  tests cannot reassign an ESM `let` export. Swap the object's field\n  and restore it in `t.cleanup`.\n- Shared helpers; import these, never re-implement:\n  `src/gocompat/` (`strings.ts`: Go TrimSpace/Ext/`%.2f`/strconv.Quote/\n  byte-order sort and `truncateUtf8`; `duration.ts`: Go durations as\n  bigint nanoseconds; `match.ts`: Go `path.Match`),\n  `src/textsafe/textsafe.ts`, `src/fsutil/atomic.ts`\n  (`writeFileAtomic`, options cover trust, credentials, and gate temp\n  names and error messages), `src/git/git.ts` (the only git runner;\n  pass the CLI context's `env`, it reads `process.env` only when none is\n  given), `src/util/pool.ts` (`mapPool`).\n\n## CLI core (`src/cli/`)\n\n- Commands are `CommandDef`s (`command.ts`) listed in `commands.ts`;\n  `run.ts` builds the yargs tree from that list plus `registerCommand`\n  (tests), and calls the handler only after parsing succeeds.\n- A handler gets a `RunContext` (cwd, env, signal, fetch, one shared\n  `LineReader`) and throws `UsageError` / `ExitSignal` / any error; it\n  never writes the error itself or reads process globals.\n- A group with `subcommands` and no handler prints its help.\n- yargs number parsing is off (`parse-numbers: false`). Declare an\n  integer flag as `type:'string'` and parse decimal digits in the\n  handler, throwing `UsageError` on a bad value (see `parseLimit` in\n  `runs.ts`).\n- Terminal detection and browser opening are swapped through\n  `terminalHooks` (`terminal.ts`).\n- With only the default `$0` command registered, yargs omits the\n  Commands section from root help; it appears once a second command\n  registers.\n\n## Review command (`src/cli/review.ts`)\n\n- End-to-end review tests use `settingsRepo` (`test/helpers/review.ts`):\n  a temp repo with an uncommitted change, a config on a fake `chat`\n  server, keys in env, `review.snapshot: false`, and approval via\n  `roast trust --yes`. It chdirs into the repo.\n- yargs keeps only the last occurrence of an array flag under\n  `duplicate-arguments-array: false`; review slice flags are re-read\n  from `ctx.argv` (`review-flags.ts`). Flags whose \"changed\" state\n  matters have no yargs default (`undefined` = not given).\n- The structured finder call offers `findings` plus the agent's\n  `__roast_continue`; assert tool presence, not exact lists.\n- The entry exits within the tick of the first SIGINT, and identical\n  signals sent back to back coalesce, so a second-signal test needs a\n  slow wind-down (a fake `git` that exits slowly on SIGTERM).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Use the `test` wrapper in `test/helpers/test.ts`, which adds Go-style\n  `t.cleanup` (tapzero has no teardown hook). tapzero's `Test` has no\n  `notOk`; write `t.ok(!x, ...)`.\n- CLI tests run in-process with `runRoast` (`test/helpers/run.ts`),\n  which makes a temp repo with an isolated env (`test/helpers/repo.ts`:\n  `tempRepo`, `tempDir`