{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLw4jb6Fp6aztbjrvQ1H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] lint, typecheck, and the TS test suite pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nReviews now capture snapshots, and every checklist item is done. `npm test` passes (6735 assertions, none failing), and so do lint, `npm run test:go` and `go build ./...`. Everything is committed in three commits; `.redeye/notes.md` is left uncommitted as instructed.\n\n1. **Snapshot module** (`src/snapshot/snapshot.ts`): it adds `pinWorktree`, `capture`, `deleteSnapshot`, the `headOid`/`revOid`/`treeOid` lookups, `liveIndexPath` and `copyIndex`. Every function takes the CLI context's `env` and `signal`, so `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is read from that env, and a relative value is resolved against the toplevel. `pinIndexTree` in `src/context/tree.ts` now uses the same two index helpers instead of its own copies.\n2. **Review integration** (`src/cli/review.ts`): a non-staged review always pins the worktree, even with `review.snapshot: false`, and every reader uses the pinned tree. If the pin fails, the review logs the documented note and reads the live tree. A `durable` flag is set right after the run record is initialized; until then, any exit deletes the captured ref.\n3. **Capture decision**: I kept the existing `src/cli/snapshot-meta.ts` (the ticket allowed it) and swapped ticket 20's placeholder for the real snapshot functions. The records serializer already orders the keys and drops empty ones, so the `meta.json` shape needed no changes.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `test/snapshot/snapshot.ts` covers the module checklist, using the \"messy repo\" fixture.\n- `test/cli/review-snapshot.ts` covers the CLI checklist.\n- To make sure the tests can fail, I turned off ref deletion and then the use of the pin, one at a time. Each change made the matching tests fail.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The CLI test for \"no HEAD\" deletes HEAD with `git update-ref -d HEAD` inside `settingsRepo`, so `main.go` stays staged.\n- On the first run, one assertion in the snapshot module tests failed while the file was being rewritten on disk. It never failed again in over 18 reruns, so I treated it as a one-off; it's recorded in the notes.\n- The built-CLI tests in `test/cli/review-errors.ts` fail against an out-of-date `dist/`. Run `npm run bundle` first; `npm test` already does.\n- `npm run test:one` sends output through tap-spec, which can crash and hide the summary when an assertion fails. Running `node test/one-bundle.js` shows the raw output.\n\nI added the reusable notes, including the last two points, to `docs/agents/scope-context.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332,"cache_read_input_tokens":148103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332},"output_tokens":773,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ad23c81-404a-48c1-af0c-22c3c0a830e9","uuid":"7094d84b-bd23-4a02-b4d4-f1c5d1d4c324","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:04:45.550Z","request_id":"req_011ChLw4jRf4C56rpF57DSj8"}
